nodes/node_projection_consumer_flow/0000_create_consumer_flow_windows.sql	nodes/node_projection_consumer_flow/0002_reconcile_consumer_flow_window_shapes.sql	OMN-16777	Both 0000 and 0001 spelled every declared-NOT-NULL column as `ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS <col> <type> NOT NULL`, which cannot reconcile a drifted table that holds rows: PostgreSQL raises 'column "<col>" of relation "<t>" contains null values' and ON_ERROR_STOP=1 kills the Job -- the same deploy-stopping failure the reconciliation exists to prevent, so tests/ci/test_node_migration_shape_reconciliation.py went GREEN while the failure class stayed open. Proven by execution on the .201 dev lane 2026-08-28 against a seeded drifted consumer_flow_windows (only consumer_group, one row): the NOT NULL spelling exits 3 on `topic`; the nullable spelling exits 0 and converges all 14 columns. Rewriting both files is safe because neither was ever applied -- to_regclass() for both relations is ABSENT on the .201 dev lane, so no content_sha256 is recorded anywhere to conflict with. [OMN-17139: the clause originally appended here, 'and onex_application_migration_manifest exists on NO .201 lane', is not evidence of anything -- that relation is a TEMP table bootstrap.sql builds per session and is absent on every lane by construction. The applied-ness question is settled only by platform_catalog.schema_migrations; probe it with scripts/migrations/check_migration_applied_on_lane.py. The conclusion above stands on the to_regclass() evidence that precedes the struck clause.] The corrected delta is re-expressed additively in 0002.
